[{"id":"wmux-report-lut6","itemId":"wide-mux","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">mux16</code> is a 16-to-1 multiplexer: <code class=\"nobreak\">y</code> is the bit of the 16-bit <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> that <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> picks. Below is the Primitives table of its Utilization report: one row for each kind of cell, with how many the design uses.","explanationHtml":"<p>Read the LUT6 row. Each LUT6 is a 4-to-1 multiplexer on four bits of <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>, so 16 bits need four. Two MUXF7s each pick between two LUT6s, and the MUXF8 picks between the MUXF7s, so <code class=\"nobreak\">y</code> comes out of the MUXF8.</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/mux16/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":180,"excerpt":["+----------+------+---------------------+","| Ref Name | Used | Functional Category |","+----------+------+---------------------+","| IBUF     |   20 |                  IO |","| LUT6     |    4 |                 LUT |","| MUXF7    |    2 |               MuxFx |","| OBUF     |    1 |                  IO |","| MUXF8    |    1 |               MuxFx |","+----------+------+---------------------+"],"ask":"How many LUT6 cells does mux16 use?","answer":"4","numeric":true},{"id":"wmux-order-path","itemId":"wide-mux","role":"stretch","promptHtml":"Vivado built <code class=\"nobreak\">mux16</code>, the 16-to-1 multiplexer, from LUT6s, MUXF7s and a MUXF8. Put in order the cells that one bit of <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> passes through on its way to <code class=\"nobreak\">y</code>.","explanationHtml":"<p>Each LUT6 chooses among four bits of <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>, a MUXF7 then chooses between two LUT6s, eight bits in all, and the MUXF8 between two MUXF7s, all sixteen. The MUXF8 must come after the MUXF7s, because it picks between their outputs. The pin buffers come first and last, as in lesson 0.3.</p>","type":"order","steps":["An IBUF brings the bit of `d` in from its pin.","A LUT6 picks one of four bits of `d`.","A MUXF7 picks between two LUT6s.","A MUXF8 picks between two MUXF7s.","An OBUF drives the pin of `y`."],"shuffled":[0,4,2,3,1]},{"id":"wmux-fill-sel","itemId":"wide-mux","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">mux16</code> is a 16-to-1 multiplexer: <code class=\"nobreak\">y</code> is the bit of the 16-bit <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> that <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> picks. Fill in the range of <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> so that it can pick every bit of <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> must count from 0 to 15, and four bits hold 16 values, so <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">[3:0]</code>. With <code class=\"nobreak\">[2:0]</code>, eight values, half of <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> could never be picked. A LUT6 has room for four data bits and two select bits, so two bits of <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> go into each LUT6, one picks in the MUXF7s and one in the MUXF8.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-06/mux16/mux16.sv","firstLine":2,"totalLines":8,"before":["module mux16 (","  input  logic [15:0] d,"],"blankLine":{"left":"  input  logic ","right":"  sel,"},"after":["  output logic        y",");","  assign y = d[sel];","endmodule"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"mux16","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"15","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] d,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]],"blankLine":{"left":[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],"right":[{"text":"  sel,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]},"after":[[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"        y","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" y ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" d[sel];","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]]},"accept":["[3:0]"],"caseSensitive":true,"blankLabel":"The range of sel"},{"id":"wmux-report-f8","itemId":"wide-mux","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">mux16</code> is a 16-to-1 multiplexer: <code class=\"nobreak\">y</code> is the bit of the 16-bit <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> that <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> picks. Below is the Primitives table of its Utilization report: one row for each kind of cell, with how many the design uses.","explanationHtml":"<p>Read the MUXF8 row. A MUXF8 picks between two MUXF7s, which between them cover the four LUT6s and so all 16 bits of <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>: one is enough, and its output is <code class=\"nobreak\">y</code>.</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/mux16/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":180,"excerpt":["+----------+------+---------------------+","| Ref Name | Used | Functional Category |","+----------+------+---------------------+","| IBUF     |   20 |                  IO |","| LUT6     |    4 |                 LUT |","| MUXF7    |    2 |               MuxFx |","| OBUF     |    1 |                  IO |","| MUXF8    |    1 |               MuxFx |","+----------+------+---------------------+"],"ask":"How many MUXF8 cells does mux16 use?","answer":"1","numeric":true}]